message: If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software

title: CEADpx/matto - Joint material and topology optimization of stimulus-responsive soft materials
abstract: CEADpx/matto is an open-source research framework for nonlinear, quasi-static finite-element analysis and gradient-based topology optimization of stimulus-responsive soft materials. Built with FEniCSx and extended from FEniTop, MatTO separates the optimization workflow from material-specific constitutive models, allowing the same filtering, adjoint-sensitivity, MMA, and nonlinear finite-element machinery to be used across different material families. The current examples include hard-magnetic soft materials, anisotropic and isotropic magnetoactive elastomers, and liquid crystal elastomers, with design fields for structural density, material composition or active-material distribution, and local material orientation.

